account.terms.n1whatyousendthemodel2thetextandimagesyourjourn = { $slot-1 }What you send the model.{ $slot-2 } The text and images your journal needs a model to work through, plus your speech when the audio switch is on. Our model processes it and returns the result. { $slot-3 }The service keeps nothing: no content is kept once your request is answered, not even in logs. No human reviews it. It is never sold, licensed, shared for anyone else's purposes, profiled, or used for advertising.{ $slot-4 }
account.terms.n1whenacanceltakeseffect2onamonthlyplanandinthe = { $slot-1 }When a cancel takes effect.{ $slot-2 } On a monthly plan, and in the first year of an annual plan, the service keeps working until the end of the period you've already paid for, then stops. We don't prorate that period, and we don't claw back. Once an annual plan has renewed, a cancel ends the service at the end of your current plan month, or at the end of that year if you'd rather. We refund one twelfth of what you paid for that renewal for each whole month left after that, the same way you paid, within 14 days of your cancel. Your plan's months start on the renewal date's day of each month, or on a shorter month's last day, and each runs until the next one starts. A withdrawal within 14 days (above) refunds everything you paid for that purchase or renewal, and sections 7, 9 and 14 name the other times we refund unused time. For confidential processing, what a plan includes within a period is part of the plan terms shown at checkout (section 13).
account.terms.n1whenitstops2cancelorletitlapseandconfidential = { $slot-1 }When it stops.{ $slot-2 } Cancel, or let it lapse, and confidential processing keeps working until your subscription ends (section 3), then stops. Withdraw within 14 days (section 3), and it stops that day. If you're a scout without a subscription and your scout access ends, it stops that day too. Closing your sign-in stops it as soon as you confirm (section 7). The service checks your access each time a connection opens, so a connection that's already open can keep working until it closes, which today takes up to forty minutes. You can subscribe anytime.
account.terms.n1whenitstops2cancelorletitlapseandtherelaykeep = { $slot-1 }When it stops.{ $slot-2 } Cancel, or let it lapse, and the relay keeps working until your subscription ends (section 3), then stops. Withdraw within 14 days (section 3), and it stops that day. Closing your sign-in stops it as soon as you confirm (section 7). Your journal, your data, and your device pairings are untouched. The free paths keep working, and you're never locked out of your own journal by a billing state. Re-subscribe anytime.
account.terms.n1whenitstops2cancelorletitlapseandthesolstonem = { $slot-1 }When it stops.{ $slot-2 } Cancel, or let it lapse, and the { $slot-3 } relay keeps carrying your traffic until your subscription ends (section 3), then stops. Withdraw within 14 days (section 3), and it stops that day. Closing your sign-in stops it as soon as you confirm, though your address can keep working until the short-lived pass your journal holds runs out (section 7). Your address stays reserved throughout. Your journal, what's in it, what you've let each agent see, and your record of what they did are all on your devices and are untouched. Re-subscribe anytime. One thing on our side, in the cases where we are the one stopping it: because this relay keeps no state, a connection already open through it closes when the short-lived pass runs out rather than at the moment we stop you, which today takes up to fifteen minutes.
